  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Trust and Cohesion in Bosnia and Herzegovina&#x2019;s Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is focusing on strengthening and promoting an environment conducive to genuine reconciliation, contributing to improved trust and social cohesion within and between communities and their leaders in Bosnia and Herzegovina. Within this framework, the project provides immediate support to key local/national stakeholders who have already been making positive moves and policies in their efforts to (i) create an environment conducive to genuine reconciliation within and between communities; and (ii) further strengthen mutual confidence, trust, constructive dialogue, understanding, empathy, respect, dignity and social cohesion. The project will be jointly implemented by the Council of Europe, the European Union, OSCE and the United Nations. National ownership will be fostered and encouraged through the collaboration and involvement of a broad array of local stakeholders. The focus will lie in empowering and strengthening coherence of civil society to lead on trust building and peacebuilding.</narrative>
  </description>
